title: 1868 Republican National Convention
subtitle: Republican Candidate for President
tags: event
view-if: year = 1868 and month = 5
max-visits: 1

= Republican National Convention

It is time to choose our candidate for President in the 1868 election. The nation stands at a crossroads, still scarred by civil war and uncertain about the future of Reconstruction. Sadly, we no longer have the steady hand and moral authority of Abraham Lincoln to unite the country and carry us to victory once more. His absence looms large over this convention, and no successor can easily fill the role he left behind.

Yet the cause is far from lost. The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican Party**</span> remains strong, tested by war and tempered by responsibility, and within its ranks stand several capable men, each offering a different vision for how the Union should be preserved and rebuilt. Though none may match Lincoln's singular greatness, each represents a path forward, and the choice we make now will shape not only the coming election, but the future of the nation itself.

- @Grant: Ulysses S. Grant
- @Wade: Benjamin Wade
- @Chase: Salmon P. Chase

@Grant
subtitle: [? if president = "Johnson": Grant is our default candidate ?]
on-arrival: {! 
    Q.Candidate = "Grant";
    Q.freedmen_rep += 2;
    Q.rural_rep += 1;
    Q.middle_class_rep += 1;
    Q.working_rep += 1;
    Q.radical_dissent -= 1;
    Q.radical_strength += 1;
    Q.moderate_dissent -= 2;
    Q.moderate_strength += 2;
    Q.conservative_dissent += 1;
    Q.conservative_strength -= 1;
    Q.liberal_dissent += 2;
    Q.liberal_strength -= 2;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/Ulysses_S._Grant_1870-1880.jpg
go-to: VP

Ulysses S. Grant is chosen as our candidate for President. His war record, humble beginnings, and willingness to support the Freedmen make him a strong choice for the party.

@Wade
subtitle: We need to convince the Party with 2 resources [? if president = "Wade": to continue his presidency?].
choose-if: resources >= 2 and conservative_strength < 26
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 2: You're broke ?][? if conservative_strength >= 26: The <span style="color: #B5651D;">**Conservatives**</span> would never allow such a Radical candidate ?]
on-arrival: {! 
    Q.resources -= 2; 
    Q.Candidate = "Wade";
    Q.freedmen_rep += 2;
    Q.rural_rep += 1;
    Q.middle_class_rep += 1;
    Q.working_rep += 1;
    Q.radical_dissent -= 2;
    Q.radical_strength += 2;
    Q.moderate_dissent += 1;
    Q.moderate_strength -= 1;
    Q.conservative_dissent += 2;
    Q.conservative_strength -= 2;
    Q.liberal_dissent += 3;
    Q.liberal_strength -= 3;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/Benjamin_F_Wade.jpg
go-to: VP

Benjamin Wade is chosen as our candidate for President. [? if president == "Wade": He will continue his leadership, much to the dismay of the <span style="color: #B5651D;">**Conservatives**</span> ?][? if president == "Johnson": His Senate career and radical ideas may appeal to the party's progressive base ?]

@Chase
subtitle: A rational option
choose-if: resources >= 2 and radical_strength < 50
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 2: You're broke ?][? if radical_strength >= 50: The <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> have a chokehold on the party and do not support Chase ?]
on-arrival: {! 
    Q.resources -= 2; 
    Q.Candidate = "Chase";
    Q.freedmen_rep += 2;
    Q.rural_rep -= 1;
    Q.middle_class_rep += 2;
    Q.working_rep -= 1;
    Q.radical_dissent += 3;
    Q.radical_strength -= 1;
    Q.moderate_dissent -= 3;
    Q.moderate_strength += 3;
    Q.conservative_dissent -= 2;
    Q.conservative_strength += 2;
!}
face-image: img/portraits/Salmon-P-Chase.webp
go-to: VP

Salmon P. Chase is chosen as our candidate. He is supported by the Old Guard and the "Anti-Grant" faction, who fear nominating a military strongman. This choice upsets the <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span>, who resent Chase [? if president == "Johnson" and House_Impeach = 1: as they believe his impartial handling of Andrew Johnson's impeachment blocked their opportunity to "railroad" the President.?].

However, some fear that Chase's history of shifting party allegiances could make him an unreliable candidate for President.

@VP

It is time to choose a running mate for our presidential candidate. The VP choice can balance the ticket and appeal to different factions of the party.

The options range from the <span style="color: #9D2933;">**Moderate**</span> choice Schuyler Colfax to more partisan candidates such as <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical**</span> Henry Wilson or <span style="color: #B5651D;">**Conservative**</span> Reuben Fenton.

- @Colfax: Schuyler Colfax
- @Wilson: Henry Wilson
- @WadeVP: Benjamin Wade
- @Fenton: Reuben Fenton

@Colfax
subtitle: **<span style="color: #9D2933;">Moderate</span>**, safe choice
face-image: img/portraits/Schuyler_Colfax,_photo_portrait_seated,_c1855-1865.jpg
on-arrival: VPCandidate = "Colfax"; moderate_strength += 2; conservative_strength += 2; radical_dissent += 1; middle_class_rep += 2; rural_rep += 1; workers_rep += 1;

Schuyler Colfax is chosen as Vice President. His **<span style="color: #9D2933;">moderate</span>** stances and Union loyalty appeal broadly to the party's mainstream and **<span style="color: #B5651D;">conservative</span>** wings, though <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> are less enthused.

His presence on the ticket reassures many Republicans that the party will remain united behind Reconstruction while avoiding unnecessary political confrontation.

@Wilson
subtitle: Strong <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical**</span> support
choose-if: radical_strength >= 30
face-image: img/portraits/Henry_Wilson,_VP_of_the_United_States.jpg
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> are not powerful enough to push Wilson
on-arrival: VPCandidate = "Wilson"; radical_strength += 3; radical_dissent -= 2; radical_dissent -= 2; workers_rep += 3; freemen_rep += 2; immigrant_laborers_rep += 1;

Henry Wilson is chosen as Vice President. His <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republican**</span> credentials and ties to labor help solidify support among progressive voters, but worry moderates.

His nomination signals a greater willingness to pursue the goals of Reconstruction with renewed energy and determination.

@WadeVP
view-if: Candidate != "Wade" and president != "Wade"
choose-if: radical_strength >= 30
face-image: img/portraits/Benjamin_F_Wade.jpg
unavailable-subtitle: [? if radical_strength < 30: The <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> lack the power to force Wade onto the ticket ?]
on-arrival: VPCandidate = "Wade"; radical_strength += 4; radical_dissent -= 4; moderate_dissent += 2; moderate_dissent += 2; freemen_rep += 3; workers_rep += 2; middle_class_rep -= 1; rural_rep -= 1;

Benjamin Wade is chosen as Vice President. His leadership among <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republicans**</span> electrifies the party's left wing, but deeply alarms moderates and conservatives.

Few doubt that Wade's selection will strengthen the influence of the <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> within the administration and the party alike.

@Fenton
subtitle: Strategic Pick: -1 Resource
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not Enough Resources
face-image: img/portraits/Reuben_Fenton_-_Brady-Handy.jpg
on-arrival: resources -= 1; VPCandidate = "Fenton"; moderate_strength += 1; NY_workers_rep += 1; NY_middle_class_rep += 1; NY_middle_class_rep += 2; NY_rural_rep += 1; NY_freemen_rep += 1; NY_immigrant_laborers_rep += 1; NY_unemployed_rep += 1;

Reuben Fenton is chosen as Vice President. As governor of New York, he will bring new energy to the campaign as the state will bring greater <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> support to New York.

His political organization and experience in New York are expected to strengthen the party's position in one of the nation's most important electoral battlegrounds.